    "created_at": "2025-10-08T20:02:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-08T20:02:49Z",
    "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/common-microsyntaxes.html#rules-for-parsing-integers also doesn't say what to do with large values, and is not only used for legacy APIs. There are also non-negative integers.\n\nI think even if the limit should be UA-defined, the spec can still say to return an error if the value overflows. But I'd also be open to specifying what the limit is for integers, at least if it's already interoperable.\n\nWebIDL has https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#numbers which applies for `long` and `unsigned long` which HTML's IDL attributes typically use for things that are parsed as integers (if there's a reflecting attribute for example). Are these limits the same as what browsers use for parsing HTML integers and HTML unsigned integers?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
