    "created_at": "2026-11-13T06:29:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T06:29:30Z",
    "body": "I don't think Infra limits freedom really applies here because we just have a straightforward spec bug where following https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content-other.html#determine-dimensions results in trying to return arbitrarily large integers from an `unsigned long` attribute.\n\nAt a minimum the spec should define what happens if _width_ or _height_ are outside the `unsigned long` range (i.e. greater than 2<sup>32</sup> &minus; 1). It could then further allow implementation-defined limits below that; WebKit and Gecko max out at 2<sup>31</sup> &minus; 1.\n\nAnd then there's the question of what is done when hitting these limits. Browsers seem to fall back to the natural dimensions.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
